# Tests and fixtures. `COPY . .` was putting every app's test package into the
# runtime image, along with the scratch scripts below — none of which the
# gunicorn process can ever reach, and all of which are extra surface.
#
# `**/tests/` rather than `tests/`: a pattern with no slash is matched against
# the context root only, and every test package here is at `apps/<app>/tests/`.
# Django's app loading imports `apps.py` and `models.py`, never `tests`, so
# `collectstatic` at build time is unaffected.
**/tests/
conftest.py
pytest.ini
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Ad-hoc scripts written against live third-party sandboxes. These carried
# hardcoded API keys, and a key in a layer of a pushed image is readable by
# anyone who can pull it — `docker history` shows the layer whether or not the
# file survives to the final stage.
test_*.py

# A captured Django debug page. Django masks settings whose names look like
# secrets, but the rest of the page is the full settings dump, the source of
# every frame in the traceback, and the request that caused it. Nothing that
# belongs in a shipped image.
#
# Named exactly, not `*.html`: the email and admin templates under `templates/`
# are .html too, and excluding those would ship an image that raises
# TemplateDoesNotExist the first time it sends a verification email.
debug_500.html

# Scratch upload fixtures.
dummy.jpg
